Z||000000||v8vinnie||01-11-2001||05:31 PM||||hey guys, tommoroww im going to finish the front end. since im going to install the upper slotted ball joints and use the stock rubber bushings, should i put both shimms in the rear to get maximum caster, or leave it the way it is, its might be easier and faster when i bring it to the alignment shop, this way the price might be lower???||||reg||6
Z||000001||88formula||01-11-2001||05:37 PM||||Those shims also adjust camber and have an effect on toe. I would leave it to the alignment shop because if camber is out they will have to mess with the shims anyway. The alignment machines they use tell them what shims to put in anyway, at least the ones I used did.||||reg||1
